From 49c268ba7384a04d2b551435411d5b4b44661f17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:14:18 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(chamfer): no-pick 2D Chamfer rides the wall, verify
 holds its tip to it

A 2D Chamfer with no picks sectioned the model at Top of Part Z and put
the cone tip on that outline at the corner depth. On a model whose edge
already carries a modelled chamfer, that outline is the bevel's top
edge, inside the wall by the bevel's width: the cone cut a V 0.7 mm into
the part, and the width moved only Z. The ride now sections the corner
depth too and rides, for each top edge, the wall loop under it within
the width (a vertical wall keeps its top loop unchanged, so sharp-edged
parts post as before); a top edge with no wall within the width refuses
by name.

The program sim credited the V as the op's declared edge break, because
the record declared that same false edge. A 2D Chamfer's records are now
credited only where the cone tip stands on a wall of the model (air
beside the tip on one side of the edge); otherwise the columns are
judged against the model and the cut is a blocking gouge.

Fixes #2435

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
